WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.056
Lukas: The previous image digest is retained locally. Its signature and retrieval path are verified.

2
00:00:07.056 --> 00:00:14.400
Raj: The clean rebuild record covers that image. But rollback uses retained bytes, not rebuilding.

3
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:22.919
Hannah: Can the old worker read current checkpoints? Image availability alone doesn't prove operational rollback.

4
00:00:22.919 --> 00:00:30.503
Anika: Yes, checkpoint format stayed unchanged this time. Just to confirm, we tested that, right?

5
00:00:30.503 --> 00:00:38.231
Priya: Okay, the smoke test passed after simulated rollback. No live production reversal is needed now.

6
00:00:38.231 --> 00:00:45.239
Raj: Maybe the callback replacement will change compatibility. We'll review it as a separate change.

7
00:00:45.239 --> 00:00:52.487
Lukas: Document draining before restoring the old lease. The rollback trigger must include duplicate writes.

8
00:00:52.487 --> 00:00:59.518
Anika: A temporary workaround would pause the partition. We'd preserve its checkpoint before any reversal.

9
00:00:59.518 --> 00:01:09.190
Hannah: The isolated rollback preserved all processed records. Unprocessed records resumed without duplicate side effects.

10
00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:17.110
Priya: Good, keep the old artifact through retention. We can close deployment, not erase recovery options.

